# Component Hardening
For public component work:
1. Read inventory, family, contract and batch state.
2. Review the family API profile.
3. Audit the public API.
4. Improve shared engines before duplicating logic.
5. Implement.
6. Add/update behavior tests.
7. Verify A11Y, SSR, cleanup, theme/RTL and package behavior as applicable.
8. Update official docs/demos.
9. Run component/family gates.
10. Update hardening state only after verification.

Audit Props, Emits, Slots, Expose, Models, Instance types, Programmatic APIs, Public types, Context/provider surface and behavioral semantics.

- Capability and maturity are separate.
- Wrapper components may be STABLE without artificial depth.
- Score never determines STABLE.
- Prefer 6-12 components from one family per batch.
